# Business layer — no DbContext

`OliveMorocco.Business` services **must not** inject or use `AppDbContext`, `DbSet<T>`, or EF APIs directly.

## Use instead

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| CRUD / queries | `IRepository<T>` (injected per entity) |
| Multi-step atomic save | `IRepository<T>.ExecuteInTransactionAsync(...)` — all repos share the scoped context |
| DTO mapping | AutoMapper profiles in `Business/Mapping/` |
| Rules | FluentValidation in `Business/Validation/` |

EF Core and `AppDbContext` live in **DataAccess** only (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`).

## Do not

- `private readonly AppDbContext _db` in a service
- `_db.Database.BeginTransactionAsync` in Business — call `Repo.ExecuteInTransactionAsync`
- `DbSet`, `Include`, `SaveChanges` in Business — extend the repository if a query pattern is missing

## Cross-aggregate example (facture + bon de livraison link)

```csharp
await Repo.ExecuteInTransactionAsync(async ct =>
{
    await Repo.AddAsync(entity, ct);
    await LinkBonsLivraisonAsync(entity.Id, prepared.ClientId, prepared.Lignes, ct);
}, cancellationToken);
```

If a repository method is missing, add it to `IRepository<T>` / `Repository<T>` in DataAccess — do not bypass with DbContext in Business.
